# A list method's copied loop over a list of numbers is IsElementPresent > Branch > GetArrayElement [isPresent] > the arrow. The test is an operation of a turn laid out: eight turns stand in a row, and the kind
# of a list in either storage of numbers is asked once in front of them. A hole leaves the loop: the first one lies at every index of ten, and nowhere: each of the eight turns, and the written loop behind them,
# is the one that leaves.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = IsElementPresent {{*}}arrayStorage=Double {{*}}admitsInt32Storage
# CHECK: = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Double level=Proven {{*}}isPresent
# The eighth turn reads its element seven elements behind the first, in either storage.
# RUN(EMIT): emit f1 mechanisms=all
# EMIT: = Load({{*}}offset = 56, indexedDoubleProperties
# EMIT: = Load({{*}}offset = 56, indexedContiguousProperties
# What plain Bun prints.
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 0,0;1,2;4,6;9,12;16,20;25,30;36,42;49,56;64,72;81,90;100,110;
